{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 performers all use scvi_n200 + multiprofile + multimodal, with config_007 (vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.7250) as the clear best. Transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool by ~0.019 (config_007 vs config_030), and weighted fusion edges out concat by ~0.004 (config_007 vs config_036). Question: config_008 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat) is the closest untested variant to the best performer, sharing the two most impactful choices (RNA encoder and image encoder). While I expect it to land around 0.70 (below config_007), it is the highest-expected-accuracy untested configuration in the proven design region and rules out any residual interaction benefit between avgpool and concat that the marginal evidence doesn't fully exclude. Why this is the best use of the final experiment: All other untested scvi_n200 multiprofile multimodal configs (config_037, config_049) swap in resnet50 and/or avgpool, making them strictly less promising. Single-profile and non-scvi_n200 configs are far below the 0.70 threshold. Since this is the last experiment, I select the configuration with the highest expected accuracy to give the best (albeit small) chance of exceeding 0.7250. Expected cost: ~4.5–5.0 GPU hours (similar to config_030's 4.82, since it shares the same encoders and uses the cheaper avgpool aggregation rather than transformer)."
}

